@startuml
title Checkout Flow Across Frontend and Backend Layers

actor Customer
participant "CheckoutPage\n(frontend)" as Page
participant "checkoutApi\n(frontend API wrapper)" as Api
participant "CheckoutController\n(API layer)" as Controller
participant "CheckoutMappingExtensions\n(mapping)" as Mapping
participant "CheckoutService\n(application layer)" as Service
participant "Repositories + PaymentService\n(application/persistence coordination)" as Modules
participant "PaymentRepository\n(simulated gateway)" as PaymentRepo
database "IUnitOfWork / Database" as Db

Customer -> Page: Confirm checkout
Page -> Page: Normalize and validate address
Page -> Api: checkout request
Api -> Controller: POST /api/checkout?currency=BRL

Controller -> Controller: Read user id from JWT
Controller -> Mapping: Map API request to application DTO
Mapping --> Controller: Application checkout request
Controller -> Service: Execute checkout

Service -> Modules: Validate cart, customer,\nlistings, stock, payment total
Service -> Modules: Create address, order\nand order items
Service -> Modules: Record checkout payment
Modules -> PaymentRepo: Add OrderPayment
PaymentRepo -> PaymentRepo: Set simulated reference,\nPaid status and paid timestamp
Service -> Modules: Deduct stock and convert cart
Service -> Db: Save checkout state
Db --> Service: Saved

Service --> Controller: Checkout response
Controller -> Mapping: Map application response to API response
Mapping --> Controller: API checkout response
Controller --> Api: 200 OK + checkout response
Api --> Page: Created order, cart, payment, total
Page -> Page: Clear local cart id
Page -> Customer: Redirect to order details

@enduml
